learning: |
  <p>Building Batrina was an advanced journey into complex app architecture and backend logic. Key technical milestones included:</p>
  <p><strong>Advanced State Management:</strong> Utilizing Cubit &amp; Provider to handle complex global states like Cart, User Profile, and Themes.</p>
  <p><strong>Complex Business Logic:</strong> Implementing a multi-dimensional inventory system (Matrix) where stock depends on both Color and Size variants.</p>
  <p><strong>Firebase Transactions:</strong> Ensuring data integrity during high-concurrency situations (e.g., two users buying the last item).</p>
  <p><strong>Deep Linking Architecture:</strong> Configuring intent filters and handling incoming links for a frictionless "Click-to-Open" experience.</p>
  <p><strong>Scalable Architecture:</strong> Designing a codebase that supports immediate switching between User and Admin modes dynamically.</p>
  <p><strong>Performance Optimization:</strong> Achieving 60 FPS through image caching, lazy loading, and efficient widget rebuilds.</p>
